FINAL ANSWER:
Two people own most of the code. Troy Goode holds 605 of 1,662 non-blank lines (36.4%), or 762 of 1,985 counting blank lines (38.4%). Douglas Christopher Wilson holds 551 non-blank lines (33.2%), or 629 counting blank lines (31.7%). Together they hold about 70% of the lines. These counts are surviving lines by blame at 62628c0, not commit counts.

| Owner | Non-blank lines (share) | Lines incl. blank (share) | Commits |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 605 (36.4%) | 762 (38.4%) | 93 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 551 (33.2%) | 629 (31.7%) | 143 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado (name garbled in the tool output) | 80 (4.8%) | 95 (4.8%) | 2 |
| Jon Church | 59 (3.5%) | 72 (3.6%) | 3 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 57 (3.4%) | 67 (3.4%) | 2 |
| Ulises Gascón | 46 (2.8%) | 52 (2.6%) | 3 |
| 39 others | 264 (15.9%) | 308 (15.5%) | n/a |

- **Commits mislead here.** Wilson has the most commits (143, 45.4%), but Goode has more surviving lines. A formatting commit, 62628c0, reindented the JS. I counted it as set aside, so its lines go back to the earlier authors and it doesn't hand ownership to whoever ran it.
- **Goode may be one person under two identities.** Troy Goode appears under `<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example`. If those are the same person, they hold 649 lines (39.0%). That is a guess from names and addresses, and I haven't applied it. A second guess is that Alejandro Caravaca Puchades and `alex94puchades` share an address.
- **The code is concentrated.** Two authors hold 50% of the lines, and it takes 5 to reach 80%.
- **Much of the code belongs to people who have gone quiet.** This is measured as of 2026-04-12, the date of the last commit. Only 9 of 44 people committed in the previous 365 days, and they hold 51.7% of the lines. The other 48.3% belongs to people with no commit in that window. That includes Wilson (33.2%) and Marquínez Prado (4.8%). Counting only active people, the bus factor is 1, which is Goode.
- **Six of 18 files are orphaned.** Their top owner is inactive and nobody active holds 20% or more. They make up 7.8% of the lines. The largest are `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml` (61 lines), `HISTORY.md` (41) and `LICENSE` (18).
- **Ownership differs by directory:**
  - `test/` is 820 lines (49.3% of the repo), and Goode holds 47.3% of it.
  - `lib/` is 214 lines (12.9%), and Goode holds 61.7% of it.
  - `.github/` is 305 lines (18.4%), and Wilson holds 30.2% of it.
  - Root files are 323 lines (19.4%), and Wilson holds 29.4% of them.
- **Some files have a single owner.** Marquínez Prado wrote `scorecard.yml` (61 lines), Beltran wrote `codeql.yml` (53), and Goode wrote `test/vary.js` (32). GitHub committed the scorecard and CodeQL files, but the lines are credited to their authors.
- **What I left out.** The counts exclude one bot, dependabot[bot] (10 lines, 11 commits). The history also begins with a 2013 import covering 44% of the files, and the table covers work since then.
